# The current Sutra demo reads no application-level environment variables and
# requires no AWS credentials. The local D1 binding is declared as `DB` in
# .openai/hosting.json and is simulated by the development stack.
#
# Keep this file free of real values. Add a documented, non-secret placeholder only
# when application code starts consuming a variable. Production secrets must be
# provisioned through environment-specific managed secret stores/KMS, never .env.
#
# Never add AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_SESSION_TOKEN, a live
# ExternalId, broker signing/encryption keys, customer role ARNs, or customer data.
